### Step 1: Bug Scenario Image Analysis & Root Cause Reasoning

**Bug Scenario Image Description:**
- The image shows an Accordion UI component with two sections.
- The chevron (expand/collapse arrow) is currently aligned to the left (start) of the heading, before the section title text.

**Bug Report Summary:**
- The request is to add an `align` prop to the Accordion, allowing the chevron to be aligned at the "start" (left, before the title) or "end" (right, after the title) of the heading.
- The default for this codebase should be "start", but the code should support both "start" and "end" alignments.

**Root Cause:**
- The current implementation always renders the chevron before the title (i.e., "start" alignment).
- There is no `align` prop in either `Accordion` or `AccordionItem`.
- There is no logic to conditionally render the chevron before or after the title based on an `align` prop.

